# An unclosed `datetime(` or `timespan(` ends at the end of its line.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where d > datetime(2024-01-01
| where e > timespan(1:00
| take 1
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..69
  PIPELINE@0..68
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..33
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..33
        NAME_REF@10..11
          IDENT@10..11 "d"
        WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
        GT@12..13 ">"
        WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
        LITERAL@14..33
          DATETIME@14..33 "datetime(2024-01-01"
    WHITESPACE@33..34 "\n"
    PIPE@34..35 "|"
    WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
    WHERE_OP@36..59
      IDENT@36..41 "where"
      WHITESPACE@41..42 " "
      BIN_EXPR@42..59
        NAME_REF@42..43
          IDENT@42..43 "e"
        WHITESPACE@43..44 " "
        GT@44..45 ">"
        WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
        LITERAL@46..59
          TIMESPAN@46..59 "timespan(1:00"
    WHITESPACE@59..60 "\n"
    PIPE@60..61 "|"
    WHITESPACE@61..62 " "
    TAKE_OP@62..68
      IDENT@62..66 "take"
      WHITESPACE@66..67 " "
      LITERAL@67..68
        LONG@67..68 "1"
  WHITESPACE@68..69 "\n"

error[DS0003]: `datetime(` is never closed
  --> query:1:15
  |
1 | t | where d > datetime(2024-01-01
  |               ^^^^^^^^^ this literal has no closing `)` on this line
  |
  = help: close it with `)`: `datetime(2024-01-01)`

error[DS0003]: `timespan(` is never closed
  --> query:2:13
  |
2 | | where e > timespan(1:00
  |             ^^^^^^^^^ this literal has no closing `)` on this line
  |
  = help: close it with `)`: `timespan(1:00)`
